"""Wheel motor bridges (2 x DRV8874) with their in-line shunts and chokes, and the fan driver
(STSPIN958) reconfigured for a drone-class motor on 4S.

Bridges, IC8 (right motor, M2) and IC9 (left motor, M1): DRV8874PWPR, one HTSSOP-16 per motor
next to its connector (TI SLVSF66A; research/next-revision, Drivetrain and A.1). The
datasheet's netlist rules are checked by components/ti/DRV8874/checks.zen in
boards/main2/test/test_drivers.zen.
- PH/EN mode, PMODE on GND (Table 2: <= 0.65 V). The timer PWM goes on EN/IN1 and the direction
  on PH/IN2: right motor Motor_Right_EN (PA8, TIM1_CH1) and Motor_Right_PH (PA9), left motor
  Motor_Left_EN (PC7, TIM3_CH2) and Motor_Left_PH (PC9). EN = 0 is the low-side brake (Table 3),
  so the bridge alternates drive and low-side slow decay at 100 kHz, the fPWM maximum (section
  6.3) and below the INA241's 125 kHz PWM-rejection limit (SBOSA30D 7.3.1.1).
- IMODE on GND: fixed off-time (25 us, ended by the next input edge, section 7.3.3.2.1) with
  automatic retry, nFAULT on real faults only (Table 6 level 1). Cycle-by-cycle mode would pulse
  nFAULT at every chop (Figure 14).
- Current regulation: ITRIP x AIPROPI = VREF / RIPROPI (equation 3). RIPROPI 2.0 kOhm 1 % (R61,
  R71) and VREF from a 5.6 kOhm / 24 kOhm divider on 3V3_D (R63/R64, R73/R74): VREF = 3.3 x
  24 / 29.6 = 2.68 V, ITRIP = 2.68 V / (2.0 kOhm x 450 uA/A) = 2.97 A typ (the research's
  2.5-3 A), IPROPI 1.34 mA at ITRIP (<= 3 mA, section 6.3). The OCP (6 A min) stays above it.
- nSLEEP of both bridges on Motors_Enable (PA10) with R49 100 kOhm to GND, so the bridges sleep
  while the MCU is in reset or halted for SWD flashing (its pins float in analog mode, RM0468
  section 11.3.1); the inputs' own 100 kOhm pull-downs (Figure 16) make 50 kOhm in parallel.
- nFAULT: open drain, both wire-ORed on Motors_nFault (PC15) with R60 10 kOhm to 3V3_D (0.33 mA,
  <= 5 mA, section 6.3).
- VM on VBAT: C82/C91 100 nF at the pin (CVM1, Table 1), four 10 uF 50 V X7R 1206 per bridge
  (C83-C86, C92-C95) within a few mm, and C87/C96 100 uF 25 V bulk (CVM2). The input ripple is
  I x sqrt(D (1 - D)), about 1-1.2 A rms per bridge at 2.4 A (research Drivetrain): the research
  asks for 2-4 x 10 uF plus a 100-220 uF low-ESR polymer. TODO: the bulk is the JVS25V100M6X4
  aluminium electrolytic (ESR about 2.4 Ohm at 120 Hz, 54 mA ripple at 120 Hz), so the four
  ceramics carry the ripple; a low-ESR polymer part (for example JIERR MA25V100M6x6, LCSC
  C46550465: 30 mOhm and 2.65 A at 100 kHz per the LCSC listing) needs a component package once
  its datasheet is in hand.
- VCP: C88/C97 100 nF X7R 50 V to VM (CVCP, 16 V or more). CPH-CPL: C89/C98 22 nF X7R 50 V
  (CFLY, VM-rated).
- IPROPI: besides RIPROPI, a DNP 0402 0 Ohm (R62, R72) to the INA241's ADC net, so the first
  prototype can compare the driver's mirror with the INA241 (fit it, and remove the INA241's
  output resistor R78/R79 on the sensors sheet; research Current sensing).
- Motor path: OUT1 -> 10 mOhm 4-terminal shunt (R65, R75, WSK2512R0100FEA, sensed by the
  INA241A2 on the sensors sheet) -> choke footprint -> motor connector pin 2; OUT2 -> pin 1.
  Forward (PH = 1, OUT1 high, Table 3) drives current from the bridge into the shunt, the
  INA241's positive direction. The connector keeps the main board's B02B-PASK.
- Chokes: L4 / L5 XAL7070-473MEC 47 uH (Isat 4.2 A at a 30 % drop, Irms 4.1 A at 40 C rise,
  DCR 97 mOhm max; Coilcraft Doc 856), above ITRIP plus the 0.41-0.62 A blanking overshoot,
  about 3.6 A. Each has a 2512 0 Ohm alternative (R66, R76) across the same two nets, DNP: the
  choke is fitted by default, because the motor's inductance at 100 kHz is unmeasured (maxon:
  30-80 % of the 1 kHz value) and without a choke at 0.3 L a 3 A ITRIP peaks at about 5.8 A,
  near the 6 A OCP minimum, with 2.1 W of ripple loss against the motor's 1.28 W budget
  (research Drivetrain). Fit the 0 Ohm instead (and leave the choke off) if the bench shows the
  motor alone keeps the ripple in budget. No capacitor across the motor: it would resonate with
  the choke (research, Series choke downsides).

Fan, IC6 (STSPIN958, DS14341 Rev 1), driving connector M3 at 400 kHz (research Fan and A.5):
- MODE1 = H, MODE2 = L, MODE3 = H: single half-bridge, parallel mode, PWM trimming (Table 8);
  OUT1/OUT2 and LSS1/LSS2 tied (section 5.4.3). PWM2/PH on GND: the load between OUT and LSS,
  low-side recirculation on limit (sections 5.6.1.2, 5.6.2.2, Figures 11 and 14). OFFSET low.
- R31 25 mOhm 1 W 1206 (HoLLR1206-1W-25mR-1%) from LSS to GND, Kelvin to the pins.
- REF from R28 22 kOhm / R29 9.1 kOhm on 3V3_D (the research's example): 3.3 x 9.1 / 31.1 =
  0.966 V; Eq. 1 (section 5.6), I_peak = VREF / (RSNS x 10) = 3.86 A, about 1.5 x a 2.5 A
  running current. The limiter is also the soft start: a locked rotor draws 13-50 A from 16.8 V
  (fan study). TODO: set REF to 1.5 x the chosen motor's running current once it is chosen.
- SR: R30 1 kOhm, 2 V/ns (Table 7: 1 k / 2.2 k / 5.6 k / 10 kOhm -> 2 / 1.2 / 0.6 / 0.3 V/ns),
  which cuts the switching loss at 400 kHz against the main board's 5.6 kOhm.
- EN/nFAULT: R27 39 kOhm to 3V3_D and C30 10 nF (Table 12), on Fan_Enable (PB14). TOFF is the
  limiter flag in PWM trimming (section 5.6.2), read on Fan_TOFF (PB13). PWM1 on Fan_PWM (PB15,
  TIM12_CH2). nSTBY on 3V3_D. V1, V2 unused.
- VS on VBAT: C34/C35 470 nF 50 V X7R 0603 at the pins (Table 12: CS 470 nF) and C36/C99 10 uF
  50 V X7R 1206, with the bridges' VBAT bulk (the research's alternative to a >= 25 V C36).
  VDD on 3V3_D with C31 220 nF; C32 100 nF CP1-CP2 and C33 1 uF VSPUMP-VBOOT (Table 12).
- Choke footprint L6, XGL5030-472MEC 4.7 uH (Isat 4.8 A at a 20 % drop, 6.7 A at 30 %; DCR
  24.5 mOhm max; Coilcraft Doc 1576), between FAN_OUT and the motor, with R77 2512 0 Ohm across
  it, DNP. The choke is fitted by default: a 1S drone motor of about 3 uH needs it even at
  400 kHz (research Q3 ripple table). Fit the 0 Ohm instead for a motor that measures above about
  4 uH. No capacitor across the fan motor.
"""

load(
    "./passives.zen",
    "C_100N_0402",
    "C_10N_0402",
    "C_10U_1206_50V",
    "C_1U_0402",
    "C_220N_0402",
    "C_22N_0402",
    "C_470N_0603_50V",
    "R_0_0402",
    "R_0_2512",
    "R_100K_0402",
    "R_10K_0402",
    "R_1K_0402",
    "R_22K_0402",
    "R_24K_0402",
    "R_25M_1206",
    "R_2K_0402",
    "R_39K_0402",
    "R_5K6_0402",
    "R_9K1_0402",
)

Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")
Resistor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Resistor.zen")
B02B_PASK = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/jst/B02B-PASK/B02B-PASK.zen")
DRV8874 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/ti/DRV8874/DRV8874.zen")
JVS25V100M6X4 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/jierr/JVS25V100M6X4/JVS25V100M6X4.zen")
STSPIN958 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/st/STSPIN958/STSPIN958.zen")
WSK2512_HIGH = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/vishay/WSK2512-HIGH/WSK2512-HIGH.zen")
XAL7070_473 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/coilcraft/XAL7070-473/XAL7070-473.zen")
XGL5030_472 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/coilcraft/XGL5030-472/XGL5030-472.zen")

VBAT = io(Power)
V3V3_D = io(Power)
GND = io(Ground)

MOTOR_RIGHT_EN = io(Net)
MOTOR_RIGHT_PH = io(Net)
MOTOR_LEFT_EN = io(Net)
MOTOR_LEFT_PH = io(Net)
MOTORS_ENABLE = io(Net)
MOTORS_NFAULT = io(Net)
MOTOR_R_SENSE_P = io(Net)
MOTOR_R_SENSE_N = io(Net)
MOTOR_L_SENSE_P = io(Net)
MOTOR_L_SENSE_N = io(Net)
CURRENT_SENSOR_RIGHT = io(Net)
CURRENT_SENSOR_LEFT = io(Net)

FAN_PWM = io(Net)
FAN_ENABLE = io(Net)
FAN_TOFF = io(Net)

FAN_OUT = Net("FAN_OUT")
FAN_MOTOR = Net("FAN_MOTOR")
FAN_LSS = Net("FAN_LSS")
FAN_CP1 = Net("FAN_CP1")
FAN_CP2 = Net("FAN_CP2")
FAN_VSPUMP = Net("FAN_VSPUMP")
FAN_VBOOT = Net("FAN_VBOOT")
FAN_REF = Net("FAN_REF")
FAN_SR = Net("FAN_SR")


def bridge(side, ic, en, ph, sense_p, sense_n, adc, motor, refs):
    """One DRV8874 with its supply, charge pump, current setting, shunt, choke and connector.

    refs: designators (cvm1, cvm2 list, bulk, cvcp, cfly, ripropi, ipropi_link, vref_top,
    vref_bottom, shunt, choke, choke_link).
    """
    vcp = Net("MOTOR_{}_VCP".format(side))
    cph = Net("MOTOR_{}_CPH".format(side))
    cpl = Net("MOTOR_{}_CPL".format(side))
    ipropi = Net("MOTOR_{}_IPROPI".format(side))
    vref = Net("MOTOR_{}_VREF".format(side))
    out1 = Net("MOTOR_{}_OUT1".format(side))
    out2 = Net("MOTOR_{}_OUT2".format(side))
    shunt_out = Net("MOTOR_{}_SHUNT".format(side))
    terminal = Net("MOTOR_{}_TERMINAL".format(side))
    DRV8874(
        name=ic,
        VM=VBAT,
        GND=GND,
        VCP=vcp,
        CPH=cph,
        CPL=cpl,
        EN_IN1=en,
        PH_IN2=ph,
        NSLEEP=MOTORS_ENABLE,
        NFAULT=MOTORS_NFAULT,
        VREF=vref,
        IPROPI=ipropi,
        IMODE=GND,
        PMODE=GND,
        OUT1=out1,
        OUT2=out2,
    )
    Capacitor(name=refs["cvm1"], P1=GND, P2=VBAT, **C_100N_0402)
    for c in refs["cvm2"]:
        Capacitor(name=c, P1=GND, P2=VBAT, **C_10U_1206_50V)
    JVS25V100M6X4(name=refs["bulk"], POS=VBAT, NEG=GND)
    Capacitor(name=refs["cvcp"], P1=vcp, P2=VBAT, **C_100N_0402)
    Capacitor(name=refs["cfly"], P1=cph, P2=cpl, **C_22N_0402)
    Resistor(name=refs["ripropi"], P1=ipropi, P2=GND, **R_2K_0402)
    Resistor(name=refs["ipropi_link"], P1=ipropi, P2=adc, dnp=True, **R_0_0402)
    Resistor(name=refs["vref_top"], P1=V3V3_D, P2=vref, **R_5K6_0402)
    Resistor(name=refs["vref_bottom"], P1=vref, P2=GND, **R_24K_0402)
    WSK2512_HIGH(name=refs["shunt"], P1=out1, S1=sense_p, S2=sense_n, P2=shunt_out)
    XAL7070_473(name=refs["choke"], P1=shunt_out, P2=terminal)
    Resistor(name=refs["choke_link"], P1=shunt_out, P2=terminal, dnp=True, **R_0_2512)
    B02B_PASK(name=motor, prefix="M", P1=out2, P2=terminal)


bridge(
    "R",
    "IC8",
    MOTOR_RIGHT_EN,
    MOTOR_RIGHT_PH,
    MOTOR_R_SENSE_P,
    MOTOR_R_SENSE_N,
    CURRENT_SENSOR_RIGHT,
    "M2",
    {
        "cvm1": "C82",
        "cvm2": ["C83", "C84", "C85", "C86"],
        "bulk": "C87",
        "cvcp": "C88",
        "cfly": "C89",
        "ripropi": "R61",
        "ipropi_link": "R62",
        "vref_top": "R63",
        "vref_bottom": "R64",
        "shunt": "R65",
        "choke": "L4",
        "choke_link": "R66",
    },
)
bridge(
    "L",
    "IC9",
    MOTOR_LEFT_EN,
    MOTOR_LEFT_PH,
    MOTOR_L_SENSE_P,
    MOTOR_L_SENSE_N,
    CURRENT_SENSOR_LEFT,
    "M1",
    {
        "cvm1": "C91",
        "cvm2": ["C92", "C93", "C94", "C95"],
        "bulk": "C96",
        "cvcp": "C97",
        "cfly": "C98",
        "ripropi": "R71",
        "ipropi_link": "R72",
        "vref_top": "R73",
        "vref_bottom": "R74",
        "shunt": "R75",
        "choke": "L5",
        "choke_link": "R76",
    },
)
Resistor(name="R49", P1=GND, P2=MOTORS_ENABLE, **R_100K_0402)
Resistor(name="R60", P1=V3V3_D, P2=MOTORS_NFAULT, **R_10K_0402)

# Fan driver.
STSPIN958(
    name="IC6",
    VS=VBAT,
    VDD=V3V3_D,
    GND=GND,
    VSPUMP=FAN_VSPUMP,
    VBOOT=FAN_VBOOT,
    CP1=FAN_CP1,
    CP2=FAN_CP2,
    OUT1=FAN_OUT,
    OUT2=FAN_OUT,
    LSS1=FAN_LSS,
    LSS2=FAN_LSS,
    V1=NotConnected(),
    V2=NotConnected(),
    PWM1=FAN_PWM,
    PWM2_PH=GND,
    EN_NFAULT=FAN_ENABLE,
    NSTBY=V3V3_D,
    MODE1=V3V3_D,
    MODE2=GND,
    MODE3=V3V3_D,
    OFFSET=GND,
    REF=FAN_REF,
    TOFF=FAN_TOFF,
    SR=FAN_SR,
)
Capacitor(name="C34", P1=VBAT, P2=GND, **C_470N_0603_50V)
Capacitor(name="C35", P1=VBAT, P2=GND, **C_470N_0603_50V)
Capacitor(name="C36", P1=VBAT, P2=GND, **C_10U_1206_50V)
Capacitor(name="C99", P1=VBAT, P2=GND, **C_10U_1206_50V)
Capacitor(name="C31", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_220N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C32", P1=FAN_CP1, P2=FAN_CP2, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C33", P1=FAN_VSPUMP, P2=FAN_VBOOT, **C_1U_0402)
Resistor(name="R27", P1=V3V3_D, P2=FAN_ENABLE, **R_39K_0402)
Capacitor(name="C30", P1=GND, P2=FAN_ENABLE, **C_10N_0402)
Resistor(name="R28", P1=V3V3_D, P2=FAN_REF, **R_22K_0402)
Resistor(name="R29", P1=GND, P2=FAN_REF, **R_9K1_0402)
Resistor(name="R30", P1=GND, P2=FAN_SR, **R_1K_0402)
Resistor(name="R31", P1=FAN_LSS, P2=GND, **R_25M_1206)
XGL5030_472(name="L6", P1=FAN_OUT, P2=FAN_MOTOR)
Resistor(name="R77", P1=FAN_OUT, P2=FAN_MOTOR, dnp=True, **R_0_2512)
B02B_PASK(name="M3", prefix="M", P1=FAN_MOTOR, P2=FAN_LSS)
